    "topic": "Biomarker/Targeted therapy",
    "trials": [],
    "answer": "B",
    "explanation": "[詳解] Reference: NCCN 2022\n(A) GIST gene mutation : KIT 80%, PDGFRA 5%–10%, SDH rare\n(B) GISTs have different response rates to imatinib based upon the tumor\nmutation status: KIT exon 9 mutations have a lower response rate and PFS\nthan exon 11 tumors at 400 mg, but dosing at 400 mg BID has been\nassociated with better PFS.\n(C) KIT exon 11 mutations are most common in GISTs of all sites\nKIT exon 9 mutations are specific for intestinal GISTs\nPDGFRA exon 18 mutations are common in gastric GISTs\nReference: devita, 11th, chap 60, p895\n(D)  Epithelioid -cell GISTs are more common in the stomach and include those\nthat are PDGFRA mutated and several SDH deficient.\nReference: devita, 11th, chap 60, p895\n(E)  Extensive surgery associated with significant morbidity (ie, total\ngastrectomy to reduce risk of recurrence in stomach) is generally not\nrecommended for SDH-deficient GIST with multifocal disease (出現在備註的一\n小段話....GIST-1)",
