    "year": 111,
    "number": 71,
    "id": "111-Q071",
    "stem": "Which of the following statements for target therapies for sarcomas are correct?\n(1) Imatinib is a potential target agent for dermatofibrosarcoma protuberans due to the presence\nof COL1A1-PDGFB fusion with resultant over-production of PDGFB\n(2) In a double-blind, phase 3 trial for patients with progressive, refractory, or symptomatic\ndesmoid tumors, sorafenib significantly prolonged progression-free survival and induced\ndurable responses.\n(3) In a double-blind, phase 3 trial for patients with advanced tenosynovial giant cell tumor\n(TGCT), Pexidartinib showed a robust tumor response in TGCT with improved patients’\nsymptoms and functional outcomes.\n(4) Tazemetostat, an oral selective EZH2 inhibitor, showed clinical activity in patients with\nadvanced epithelioid sarcoma characterized by loss of INI1/SMARCB1.\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n----------",
    "options": {
      "A": "(1)(2)(3)",
      "B": "(1)(3)",
      "C": "(2)(4)",
      "D": "(4)",
      "E": "(1)(2)(3)(4)"
    },
    "sourcePage": null,
    "cancer": "GI",
    "topic": "Metastatic",
    "trials": [],
    "answer": "D",
    "explanation": "答案(4)\n根據 NCCN soft tissue sarcoma guideline\n如遇 soft tissue sarcoma，應先問是否是屬於特殊subtype，因有histology-specific 專一性的治療。\n若不屬於特殊 subtype，unresectable/metastasis 有一二標準治療:\n一線: Anthracycline-based regimens (Gemcitabine-based 為 recommended regimens)\n二線: Pazopanib, or Eribulin (Liposarcoma), or Trabectedin (Lipo/Leiomyosarcoma)\n\n而此題考的是有特殊治療的 sarcoma subtype，列出NCCN 的 prefer regimen 如下:\nDesmoid tumor (Aggressive fibromatosis) Sorafenib\nNon-pleomorphic rhabdomyosarcoma Vincristine, Dactinomycin, Cyclophosphamide\nAlveolar soft part sarcoma Pembrolizumab +- Axitinib, Sunitinib, Pazopanib\nAngiosarcoma Paclitaxel or anthracycline-based chemotherapy\nCutaneous angiosarcoma Pembrolizumab\nDermatofibrosarcoma Protuberans with\nFibrosarcomatous transformation\nImatinib\nEpithelioid sarcoma Tazemetostat\nExtraskeletal osteosarcoma Platinum-based therapy\nInflammatory myofibroblastic tumor with ALK\ntranslocation\nALK inhibitors\n(Crizotinib/Ceretinib/Brigatinib/Lorlatinib)\nMalignant perivascular epithelioid cell tumor\n(PEComa)\nAlbumin-bound sirolimus\nRecurrent angiomyolipoma,\nLymphangioleiomyomatosis\nSirolimus, Everolimus, Temsirolimus\nSolitory fibrous tumor Bevacizumab + Temozolomide, Sunitinib,\nSorafenib, Pazopanib\nTenosynovial Giant Cell tumor Pexidartinib\nWell-differentiated/De-differentiated\nliposarcoma\nPalbociclib (CDK amplified only)\n\n(1) 出自2015 AACR “Efficacy and Biological Activity of Imatinib in Metastatic Dermatofibrosarcoma\nProtuberans (DFSP)”，收了10 個病患，用FISH 發現全部都有 COL1A1-PDGFB 的 fusion gene，\n10 位病患使用Imatinib 其中 8 位有 response(ORR: 80%)，1 位 SD。\n(2) 出自NEJM 2018”Sorafenib for Advanced and Refractory Desmoid Tumors”，Phase III trial 隨機\n分配87 位病患至 Sorafenib 400mg QD 或是placebo，Primary endpoint 是 PFS。\n ORR PFS Time to response\nSorafenib 33% NE (HR 0.13) ** 9.6M\nPlacebo 20% 11.3M 13.3M\n(3) 出自ENLIVEN trial (The Lancet 2019, phase III) ，Tenosynovial giant cell tumor 會分泌 Colony\nstimulating factor 1 (CSF-1)，而Pexidartinib 是一種小分子口服TKI，作用在CSF-1 receptor 上\n及抑制KIT, FLT-3，此trial 各收錄60 位病人分別入Pexidartinib 及Placebo，而Primary endpoint\n為 ORR。\n ORR Stable disease Side effect\nPexidartinib 39% 39% Elevated liver function,\nHypertension,\nHand-foot reaction\nPlacebo 0% 78%\n(4) Epithelioid sarcoma 有 90%有 INI-1 loss(Encoded by SMARCB1)，而INI-1 loss 會造成下游 EZH2\n的不受抑制，而EZH2 增強會增加 H3Kme7，進而抑制cell differentiation，因此EZH2 被視為\n是 tumor oncogene，Tazemetostat 是小分子 TKI 可抑制 EZH2，在 phase II basket trial (Lancet\nOnco 2020), 用於治療 60 位 Epithelioid sarcoma 的病患，Primary endpoint 是 ORR。\n ORR PFS OS AE\nTazemetostat 15% 5.5M 19M Anemia, weight loss\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
