    "number": 74,
    "id": "111-Q074",
    "stem": "Recently, PROpel study has been published in NEJM Evid on line in Jun, 2022. The study will\nchange the standard treatment in prostate cancer. Which of following statements regarding to\nPROpel study are correct?\n(1) The target population is metastatic hormone sensitive prostate cancer.\n(2) The study demonstrates a combined antitumor effect when olaparib is combined with\nnext-generation hormonal agent abiraterone to treat metastatic prostate cancer as the first line\ntreatment.\n(3) The benefit is respective of homologous recombination repair gene mutation status.\n(4) Abiraterone combined with olaparib significantly prolonged imaging-based PFS compared with\nabiraterone and placebo.",
    "options": {
      "A": "(1)(2)(3)",
      "B": "(1)(3)",
      "C": "(2)(4)",
      "D": "(4)",
      "E": "(1)(2)(3)(4)"
    },
    "sourcePage": null,
    "cancer": "GU",
    "topic": "Metastatic",
    "trials": [],
    "answer": "C",
    "explanation": "答案: (C)\n(1) The target population is metastatic hormone sensitive prostate cancer. >>錯誤，研究對象為\ncastration-resistant prostate cancer\n(2) The study demonstrates a combined antitumor effect when olaparib is combined with\nnext-generation hormonal agent abiraterone to treat metastatic prostate cancer as the first line\ntreatment. >>正確\n(3) The benefit is respective of homologous recombination repair gene mutation status. >>錯誤，無\n論同源重組修復基因突變 (HRRm) 狀態如何，患者均被納入 [Patients were enrolled regardless\nof homologous recombination repair gene mutation (HRRm) statu]s\n(4) Abiraterone combined with olaparib significantly prolonged imaging-based PFS compared with\nabiraterone and placebo. >>正確\n*Reference: PROpel: Aa double-blind, phase 3 trial of abiraterone and olaparib versus abiraterone\nand placebo in patients with mCRPC in the first-line setting\nPublished June 3, 2022, NEJM Evid 2022; 1 (9)",
