    "answer": "B",
    "explanation": "ANS: B\n\n(1) 正確, IMbrave 150, Atezolizumab + Avastin v.s. sorafenib (mPFS:6.8 v.s. 4.3, p<0.001; mOS: 19.2\nv.s. 13.4m, p=0.0009)\n(2) 錯誤, REFLECT trial conclusion: Lenvatinib is “noninferior” to sorafenib (not superior)\n• Open-label, phase 3, multicentre, non-inferiority trial, CP-A, unresectable HCC pts\n• Lenvatinib v.s. sorafenib\n• Primary endpoint: OS (mOS: 13.6 v.s. 12.3 → meeting criteria for non-inferiority)\n(3) 正確, Reach2 trial conclusion: Improves OS for ramucirumab v.s. placebo in pts with HCC and\nAFP>400 s/p sorafenib as 1st line.\n• Randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled, phase 3 trial, CP-A, BCLC-B or C, AFP>400,\npreviously received sorafenib\n• Ramucirumab v.s. placebo\n• Primary endpoint: OS (mOS: 8.5 v.s. 7.3m, p=0.0199)\n• 時空背景: 2015 年 REACH trial (Phase 3, 設定與REACH2 相同不過沒有限 AFP level → Fail\n(OS, HR:0.87, p=0.14). 但在 subgroup analysis AFP > 400 的組別有看到效果 (mOS: 7.8 ->\n4.2m, p=0.006), 因此又做了 REACH2 Trial\n(4) 錯誤, The trial using Nivo+ ipi as 1st line (Checkmate 9DW) is still ongoing.\n• Checkmate 9DW: phase 3, nivo+ Ipi v.s. sorafenib or Lenvatinib as 1st line of pts with advanced\nHCCs\n• Checkmate 459: Phase 3, nivo v.s. sorafenib, 1st line, CP-A, advanced HCC\n• Primary endpoint: OS (16.4 v.s. 14.7m, p=0.075), but favourable safety profile\n→ NCCN guideline 建議if ineligible to TKI or other anti-angiogenic agents 可以使用(category 2B)\n• 2nd line data → Checkmate 040: Phase I/II, Nivo + Ipi in advanced HCC s/p sorafinib",
