    "answer": "D",
    "explanation": "ANS: D\n\nHigh-risk features (exclusive of those cancers that are MSI-H):\n• Poorly differentiated/undifferentiated histology, lymphatic/vascular invasion, bowel\nobstruction, <12 lymph nodes examined, perineural invasion, localized perforation, or close,\nindeterminate, positive margins, or tumor budding.\n• In high-risk stage II patients, there are no data that correlate risk features and selection of\nchemotherapy\n題幹問題為 High risk stage II colon cancer adjuvant chemotherapy 如何選擇\n• FOLFOX 6m [MOSIAC trial, N Engl J Med 2004; 350:2343-2351]\n• CAPOX 3m [IDEA trial high-risk stage II analysis, J Clin Oncol. 2021 Feb 20;39(6):631-641.]\n• Capecitabine or 5-FU/leucovorin 6m [Cochrane Database Syst Rev. 2008 Jul\n16;2008(3):CD005390.]\no Trials 與此主題相關的很多，結論正反皆有。Stage II surgical alone 5-year PFS 就\n有 75-80%，survival 差異較難體現。Meta-analysis 做起來 OS 沒有差異，DFS 有些\n微進步。Trials 之間 high risk definition 定義也有差異，但Capecitabine or\n5FU/leucovorin 是合理選擇。\n• Observation [Evidence adjuvant chemotherapy in stage II patients is still relatively low, so OBS\nis another option]\nOther reference: J Clin Oncol. 2022 Mar 10;40(8):892-910.",
