    "answer": "A",
    "explanation": "ANS: A\n\n(1) Resectable metachronous metastases 仍是以 resection 為主\n(2) 正確\n(3) 錯誤，根據beacon CRC trial [N Engl J Med 2019; 381:1632-1643; Uptodate: J Clin Oncol. 2021\nFeb 1;39(4):273-284.]\n⚫ Phase 3, RCT, 2-3 line treatment, mCRC with BRAF V600E mutation\n⚫ Three arms: encorafenib + binimetinib + Cetuximab v.s. encorafenib + cetuximab v.s.\ninvestigator’s choice(control group)\n⚫ Primary endpoint: OS and ORR in the triple therapy group v.s. control group\n⚫ mOS = 9.3 v.s. 9.3 v.s. 5.9m ; ORR: 26.8% v.s. 19.5% v.s. 1.8%\n⚫ FDA approve Encorafenib + cetuimab + binimetinib first, but after final data revealed →\nFDA approved Encorafenib + cetuximab +/- binimetinib\n(4) 錯誤， 被納入 FDA approval 的藥物有最早的Vemurafenib 和後來的 dabrafenib +\ntrametinib， 不過兩者皆為phase II trial, 證據力不若phase III 之beacon CRC study, 且doublet\ntherapy (encorafenib + cetuximab) side effects 小於上述兩種治療，因此 NCCN guideline 沒寫\n上 vemurafenib 和 dabrafenib + trametinib 兩種BRAF inhibitor 組合 [SWOG S1406 and J Clin\nOncol. 2015;33(34):4023–31.]",
